00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.980
Let's start with Gravelord Nito, who has had relatively little screen time

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.920
considering his immense power over death and the dead.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.520
For now, I want to prove just how relevant he is as a character,

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.320
starting with one important item that's often overlooked.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.000
It's the Effigy Shield found upon a corpse in the catacombs

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:02.340
In Dark Souls, the occult is more accurately defined as this heretical dark magic

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:08.500
used by pagans who are unaligned with and hostile to the gods.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.880
Gwyn and co. rightly fear the occult just as the dead fear the divine.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.120
It's effective against their following and kin.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.640
Nito's power isn't based on the occult.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:24.020
So if these cultists were interested in the power of Nito,

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:28.800
it follows that Nito's power over death extends to the gods as well,

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.080
and could easily be used as a weapon against them.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.660
After all, the Dragon Eye item states

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:39.400
to be alive is to be vulnerable, and the fiery gods are no exception.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.100
This tells us that Nito had power over the gods

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.480
Leverage, and where there's that much leverage, there is a huge story to be told here,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.820
but it'll have to wait until we remaster the Prepare to Cry series I think for that one.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:53.960
In the end, though

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:57.880
it's probably going to be the story of this immensely powerful entity,

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:03.360
who just wants to be left in peace at the end of the day like the rest of the Dead.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.260
Nito was the first of the Dead,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.260
as in he was the first to die when the Age of Disparity began.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.940
Before, it's unclear if there was even the concept of death.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:19.180
However, at the complete other end of the spectrum was High Lord Wolnir,

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:23.840
who wished to outlive all others and become the last of the Dead.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.120
To this end, he sentenced a great many souls to death,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.340
and he conquered the lords of many kingdoms,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.500
and he expanded the mighty kingdom of the Sands known as Carthus

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:42.740
Wolnir and Carthus deserve their own video, too, and they'll be featured really soon, so subscribe for that.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:46.040
Theirs is this story of victory at any cost,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:52.720
and that ethos, that victory at any cost, it characterizes their entire story, and it's a great one

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.640
Right now though, in this video, the curiosity I want to talk about is

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.780
why we don't see their enormous sand kingdom in-game.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.840
Because it should be right above the Catacombs of Carthus, right?

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.560
But it's not.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.830
Instead, above the catacombs of Carthus,

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.520
we have Farron and the Abyss Watchers,

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:17.120
and the reason for this is likely the convergence of the lands.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.060
If you didn't know, the lands of Dark Souls 3 are converging together,

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.660
most likely in response to the Lords not sitting on their thrones.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.900
Almost as if the world is pulling them towards it.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.540
This explains the skewed geography of Dark Souls 3,

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.640
especially the skewed geography of the Kiln or the Dreg Heap,

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.880
but I want to go a step further with this theory,

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:44.140
in regards to which lands sometimes become neighbors or next to each other.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.460
For example, I think the Abyss Watchers are specifically above Carthus

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.980
because they are the ones that put an end to that kingdom.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.080
I think they're linked to it.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:59.540
According to Hawkwood, after all, the Abyss Watchers will bury a kingdom

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.920
at the first sign of exposure,

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:07.740
and Carthus was literally a kingdom that was buried by the Abyss Watchers.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.860
The legacy of their kingdom ended up being confined to the Catacombs,

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.180
where that Abyss first appeared,

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:19.620
and perhaps that battle to crush Carthus was also the last battle of the Abyss Watchers,

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:24.540
And as the lands converged, causality sort of linked these two kingdoms together.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:29.380
Fate often works this way in Dark Souls, and I wouldn't be surprised if this was true.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.720
Speaking of fate,

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.260
let's talk about the Wolf Knight Set,

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:36.120
originally worn by Artorias the Abyss Walker.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.440
It reads,

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.560
That last part isn't actually an accurate translation.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.640
In Japanese, instead of the armor suggesting their eventual end,

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:02.900
the Abyss Watchers actually saw their own final moments in the armor.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.140
The difference being that they were actually

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:09.040
keenly aware of this Abyss-soaked fate that awaited them.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.260
This gives way more flavor to these characters

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:17.060
because having an iron will was a famed characteristic of Artorias,

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:19.620
and his abyss watchers lived up to that.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.080
They persisted in their duty,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.440
fully aware that they were literally fighting against their own inevitable fate.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.040
That is an iron will that is worth being commended for.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:37.220
Another interesting nuance of the Japanese translation is the actual name of the Followers of Farron.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:42.540
These were the Hollows or the Undead that trudged after the Undead legion,

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:46.780
disposing of any stragglers who ended up falling to the Abyss,

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.860
but these Followers of Farron more accurately called

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.180
ghosts, revenants or spirits in Japanese,

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:58.040
which really suits them for as we know from before,

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:02.680
those in the Undead Legion have already seen their inevitable demise.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.380
They're already ghosts.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.140
Their fate to die is who they are,

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.160
which really suits the definition of revenant or specter or ghost.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:16.380
And if you're a member of the undead Legion and you have partaken of the Old Wolfblood,

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.220
perhaps falling to the Abyss isn't the only grisly fate that awaits you.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.300
This is something that passed me by for the longest time.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:29.280
So from what I hear, these creatures are called Lycanthropes,

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.160
in the official guides for the game.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.940
Lycanthrope means wolf-possessed,

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.340
and seeing as this is the Farron Swamp,

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:40.720
it follows that being wolf-possessed would have something to do with the Wolf Blood

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.940
that the Abyss Watchers are willingly partaking in.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:48.400
It seems as if there's a potential negative side effect of this blood.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:50.360
Something that turns one into a beast,

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:53.560
not dissimilar to what happens in Bloodborne.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:58.280
In addition, the Hollows here are called Hunters of the Possessed,

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:03.220
and they're probably also responsible for the crucifixion that's taking place.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.680
And it turns out those crosses make pretty good chairs.

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:13.549
Orbeck was once a Vinheim scholar, although he likens it to being more of an assassin than a scholar.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:18.736
He expresses a lot of resentment for the lack of sorcery he ended up getting taught.

00:07:18.736 --> 00:07:20.810
"What a fool I was, thinking one day

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.060
I would learn real sorceries.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.969
When I became undead, I was exiled from the School.

00:07:26.849 --> 00:07:28.849
But here I am now,

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:32.680
exploring the depths of sorcery."

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.549
The nation of Vinheim and, by extension, their

00:07:35.549 --> 00:07:36.859
White Dragon School is

00:07:37.469 --> 00:07:42.319
a pretty violent place. Note how they have all these aggressive and duplicitous

00:07:42.899 --> 00:07:44.550
sorceries to their name.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.879
Hell, even Big Hat Logan, a

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:55.600
complete social recluse, is famed for his magical arsenal that emulates weaponry like swords and spears and shields.

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:01.440
So you would think that there would have been some event in this nation's history that

00:08:01.789 --> 00:08:06.999
warranted such war-based magic development, and it's for this reason that Vinheim

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:11.889
becomes our most likely victim of a war with the Way of White.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:17.799
The miracle Magic Barrier explains that there was a short period in history where

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:21.069
clerics and sorcerers opposed one another.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:25.960
It was for this reason that even the most common Way of White cleric

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:29.940
found it necessary to cast some form of Magic Barrier,

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:33.500
and so this more simple, common version of the barrier

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.320
was derived from Havel's

00:08:35.719 --> 00:08:37.719
original Great Magic Barrier.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:42.400
Oddly, the persecution of sorcerers in Dark Souls II

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:46.220
crops up in an item description you really wouldn't expect it to.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:50.920
It appears in the Varangian Sword description in Dark Souls II.

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:54.820
If you've forgotten (and no one's gonna blame you if you have),

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:59.500
the Varangians were the pirates that Vendrick forced into hard labor

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.000
at No Man's Wharf - and

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.609
it's only mentioned in a couple of descriptions,

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:07.732
but there was actually a campaign to restrain and capture them

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:11.380
because they were terrorizing the Northern Seas,

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.676
as well as hunting sea monsters, apparently.

00:09:14.676 --> 00:09:15.980
"Beyond these seas,"

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.780
this description reads,

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:22.180
"is an unexplored continent said to be the home of things inhuman."

00:09:22.339 --> 00:09:28.440
I'm always really intrigued by these parts of the Souls series that we only hear of and we never really see,

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:33.430
and, in my opinion, if there was ever to be a Dark Souls IV, one of the few ways

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:38.859
they could go forward is by fulfilling Aldritch's visions of the age of the Deep Sea

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:44.770
And this is our only mention of sea monsters that might be prepared

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:48.620
for the world that might exist in that time.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:53.000
Not all people were as easily conquered as the Varangians were, however.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:59.140
Throughout all of the stories, Mirrah remains one of the most resilient nations,

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.280
even though they're said to be constantly at war with their neighbors.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.700
Mirrah had a couple of things that were worth protecting.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:10.160
One was the Holy Water of Mirrah, which was this ancient well

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:13.640
that is said to have retained its divinity throughout all these years.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.800
Its water scalds the skin of Hollows and Undead,

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.520
and I always wondered why Hollow-fearing people like Vendrick

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:26.080
didn't make a concentrated effort to acquire this holy water.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.580
Because Vendrick definitely did have his eyes on the wonders of Mirrah.

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:32.170
In addition to their holy water,

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:35.229
there was also the wonder known as Geisteel,

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:39.159
which was this precious alloy that was created within their country and

00:10:39.589 --> 00:10:41.720
mastered by the blacksmith Llewellyn.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.589
Instead of conquering Mirrah to obtain it, however,

00:10:45.139 --> 00:10:47.439
Vendrick simply bought out the blacksmith.

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.260
He offered him an obscene amount of money,

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:53.469
and so geisteel was introduced to Drangleic.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:59.919
But more than their steel and their holy water, Mirrah was known for its Knightly code of honor.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:04.120
Such was their legend that even the peasantry dreamed of becoming knights,

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:09.459
but their chances are said to have been about 1 in 10,000.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:14.200
There's another famous success story told in exactly the same way,

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.140
except it takes place in Forossa,

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.619
and it's about Shieldless Lothian,

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:23.360
who was this fearless warrior who was born a peasant and rose to the rank of general.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:28.460
Such was his determination that he always fought without a shield on the battlefield,

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:32.100
so he always went to battle at risk of his own life,

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:35.289
and it's no surprise that that inspired his men.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:36.410
However,

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.660
one day he disappeared,

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:43.930
and one theory supplies that he tired of how frail human opponents were, and

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:47.529
he went on instead to slay the dragons of legend.

00:11:47.529 --> 00:11:52.580
His axe is imbued with lightning and it appears to support that theory.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.000
After this, however,

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.340
Forossa was destroyed by war,

00:11:56.340 --> 00:12:00.740
and its people scattered to a bunch of other lands as sellswords.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.900
Makes you wonder what would have happened,

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.180
if he didn't run off to slay dragons.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.720
The dragons aren't so easily conquered.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:12.660
Even dragons that were tamed throughout the generations in Lothric

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:19.180
appear to have turned on their own fortress as soon as there were no sane knights to keep them in check.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:26.420
Amongst the ruins of this place, Lothric had one final secret that we've kind of only really uncovered now.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:31.180
Remember how we mentioned the convergence of lands earlier,

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:34.699
when we were talking about the kingdom of Carthus and how its catacombs

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.480
drifted closer with Farron up above them?

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:43.420
Well, the Japanese description for the straightsword of the Lothric Knights states,

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:45.960
"It is said that the Lothric Knights,

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.290
along with their flying dragons,

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:51.360
